The declining birthrate of the 2010s continued to shape politics in the 2020s. Population growth slowed, and the country became more dependent on immigration and foreign labour than it had been in earlier decades. The issue was no longer whether Guajicutea could keep growing quickly, but how it would adapt to slower growth, an older society, and a more expensive housing market.

